OL,3,CHarry Kane crowned first English
OL,4,CBallon d'Or winner in 25 years
OL,6,FFurther chaos followed with the awards
OL,7,Fpushed back by 30 minutes to start at
OL,8,F8.30pm, but just over two hours later
OL,9,Fand Kane received the 70th Ballon d'Or
OL,10,Fto enormous cheers and chants of
OL,11,F'Harry' inside the London Palladium,
OL,12,Fminutes after London City midfielder
OL,13,FAlexia Putellas claimed the women's
OL,14,Fprize for a third time.
OL,16,F"Wow, I'm almost speechless," an
OL,17,Femotional Kane said on stage.
